{"parentUuid":"f9352011-8472-473e-af5c-c096c214862e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a6c24b41b58cd6945","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ke2MceNzudmC4hSnCogEv3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT sat_parameters add_rlt_cuts experimental binary clauses\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"SatParameters in cp_sat::proto - Rust\",\"url\":\"https://docs.rs/cp_sat/latest/cp_sat/proto/struct.SatParameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about the `add_rlt_cuts` parameter in CP-SAT:\n\nThe `add_rlt_cuts` parameter is still experimental but can help on binary problems with a lot of clauses of size 3, and it is set to true by default.\n\nThis parameter is part of the CP-SAT solver's SAT parameters configuration in Google's OR-Tools library. It relates to Reformulation Linearization Technique (RLT) cuts, which are advanced cutting planes used to strengthen the solver's linear relaxations when dealing with binary constraint satisfaction problems that contain many ternary (3-clause) constraints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"06ecf0fe-fa97-40bb-8089-47f545ded3cb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:41.448Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f9352011-8472-473e-af5c-c096c214862e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"39690db1-a02c-4bef-8248-053f31aa8bc1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a6c24b41b58cd6945","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CnspSiz7gcmkRvC9Cvaz3z","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RLT-POS polynomial programming software Sherali quadratic assignment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"RLT-POS: Reformulation-Linearization Technique-based optimization software for solving polynomial programming problems | Mathematical Programming Computation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-016-0099-5\"},{\"title\":\"RLT-POS: Reformulation-Linearization Technique-based optimization software for solving polynomial programming problems | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/293043079_RLT-POS_Reformulation-Linearization_Technique-based_optimization_software_for_solving_polynomial_programming_problems\"},{\"title\":\"Reformulation–Linearization Techniques for Mixed-Discrete Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-1-4614-6624-6_45-1\"},{\"title\":\"RLT-POS: Reformulation-Linearization Technique-based Optimization Software for Solving Polynomial Programming Problems | Argonne Leadership Computing Facility\",\"url\":\"https://alcf.anl.gov/events/rlt-pos-reformulation-linearization-technique-based-optimization-software-solving-polynomial\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v233y2014i3p488-499.html\"},{\"title\":\"Global Optimization of Nonconvex Polynomial Programming Problems Having Rational Exponents | Journal of Global Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1008249414776\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT cuts for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2012/01/3303/\"},{\"title\":\"RLT: A unified approach for discrete and continuous nonconvex optimization - Annals of Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10479-006-0107-7\"},{\"title\":\"Software Search - zbMATH Open\",\"url\":\"https://zbmath.org/software/18321\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713008308\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about RLT-POS and its connection to polynomial programming and the quadratic assignment problem:\n\n## RLT-POS Software\n\nRLT-POS is a Reformulation-Linearization Technique-based open-source optimization software for solving polynomial programming problems. The software includes algorithms such as constraint filtering techniques, reduced RLT representations, semidefinite cuts, and bound-grid-factor constraints.\n\n## Developers and Publication\n\nThe software was developed by Dalkiran and Sherali and published in Mathematical Programming Computation in 2016.\n\n## Key Features\n\nThe backbone of RLT-POS includes constraint filtering techniques, reduced RLT representations, and semidefinite cuts. The software has been compared with other optimization packages including BARON, COUENNE, and SparsePOP.\n\n## Connection to Quadratic Assignment\n\nThe search results show that RLT has been studied for specific problems including the standard quadratic program and the quadratic assignment problem (QAP). The Reformulation-Linearization Technique provides a way to compute a hierarchy of linear programming bounds on the optimal values of NP-hard combinatorial optimization problems, which includes applications to the quadratic assignment problem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6b0fccae-9881-4f1d-8b65-abb7dc3e48a5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:44.078Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39690db1-a02c-4bef-8248-053f31aa8bc1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d03299ec-b3db-4a0a-ac66-fabedba805dc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a6c24b41b58cd6945","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HocMz5JCunwXYzfpdGVqWa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"facility layout problem quadratic assignment RLT lift project tighter relaxation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713008308\"},{\"title\":\"Quadratic Assignment Problem (QAP)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/quadratic-assignment-problems-qap\"},{\"title\":\"Strong RLT1 bounds from decomposable Lagrangean relaxation for some quadratic 0–1 optimization problems with linear constraints\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v286y2020i1d10.1007_s10479-018-3092-8.html\"},{\"title\":\"RLT insights into lift-and-project closures | Optimization Letters | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11590-014-0763-5\"},{\"title\":\"A new relaxation framework for quadratic assignment problems based on matrix splitting | Mathematical Programming Computation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-010-0012-6\"},{\"title\":\"Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for the quadratic assignment and standard quadratic optimization problems\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v233y2014i3p488-499.html\"},{\"title\":\"facility layout problem: Topics by Science.gov\",\"url\":\"https://www.science.gov/topicpages/f/facility+layout+problem\"},{\"title\":\"[1304.0267] Improving Lower Bounds for the Quadratic Assignment Problem by applying a Distributed Dual Ascent Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.0267\"},{\"title\":\"Facilities Layout Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/rwe/10.1007/978-0-387-74759-0_171\"},{\"title\":\"A new mixed integer programming formulation for facility ...\",\"url\":\"https://eng.auburn.edu/~aesmith/files/Anewmixed%20integer%20programming%20formulation%20for%20facility%20layout%20design%20using%20flexible%20bays.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding facility layout problems, quadratic assignment problems (QAP), and RLT (Reformulation-Linearization Technique) with lift-and-project relaxations:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**RLT and Lift-and-Project Strategy:**\nThe 'lifting' refers to the addition of new variables, and the 'projection' to projecting the optimal values of the new variables to a feasible point. An inequality of this type is known as a first-level RLT cut in the variables x and X. This process may be repeated to obtain level two RLT cuts, etc.\n\n**QAP and Facility Layout:**\nThe RLT has been studied for the standard quadratic program and the quadratic assignment problem (QAP). QAP has numerous applications such as backboard wiring, scheduling problems, economic problems, designing typewriter keyboards, facility layout, and assembling printed circuit boards.\n\n**Tighter Relaxations:**\nThe second level RLT relaxation of the QAP often provides significantly better bounds than the first level RLT relaxation, but that it is computationally very expensive to solve. Additionally, RLT-3, though tighter, requires extreme memory (up to 700GB).\n\n**Exploiting Symmetry:**\nIn the presence of suitable algebraic symmetry in the original problem data, it is sometimes possible to compute level two RLT bounds with additional linear matrix inequality constraints.\n\n**Practical Challenges:**\nThe application of the Reformulation Linearization Technique (RLT) to the Quadratic Assignment Problem (QAP) leads to a tight linear relaxation with huge dimensions that is hard to solve.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8de267cd-3280-466e-bf55-f574caa0a438","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:47.902Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d03299ec-b3db-4a0a-ac66-fabedba805dc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"61e2ab50-8314-4d4a-beb1-ee1b68d69f08","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a6c24b41b58cd6945","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShSRSMk8VbMWQXe66dEskW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"combinatorial Benders decomposition logic-based RLT cuts strengthening master\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-53969-5_3\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening Techniques in Logic-Based Benders’ Decomposition | Operations Research Forum | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders’ Cuts | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-25960-2_14\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/combinatorial-benders-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"Solving logic-based benders decomposition master problems with constraint programming and domain-independent dynamic programming | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-025-09382-1\"},{\"title\":\"Combining optimisation and simulation using logic-based Benders decomposition - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S037722172300591X\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/386592005_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220244181_Combinatorial_Benders'_Cuts_for_Mixed-Integer_Linear_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/378249676_Speeding_Up_Logic-Based_Benders_Decomposition_by_Strengthening_Cuts_with_Graph_Neural_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-based-benders-decomposition-lbbd-4e47b3ae-690a-44a4-9d80-a191b385b4e6\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about combinatorial Benders decomposition, logic-based methods, RLT cuts, and strengthening master problems:\n\n## Overview\n\nLogic-based Benders' decomposition (LBBD) is a generalization of classical Benders' decomposition that extends this mathematical programming approach to problems where the subproblem is an optimization problem of any form, removing the requirement of linear programming subproblems.\n\n## Combinatorial Benders Cuts\n\nCombinatorial Benders cuts are polyhedral constraints derived from explicit combinatorial analysis of discrete problem structure within Benders decomposition frameworks. In contrast to classical (duality-based) Benders cuts, which leverage dual information of continuous or LP subproblems, combinatorial Benders cuts exploit primal infeasibility, logic, or minimal combinatorial conflict to produce strong, problem-specific valid inequalities.\n\n## Cut Strengthening\n\nCut-strengthening techniques have a significant impact on the computational effectiveness of the logic-based Benders' decomposition (LBBD) scheme, though very little has been understood about which techniques achieve the best computational performance. Computational studies involving 3000 problem instances show that cut-strengthening techniques that generate irreducible cuts outperform the greedy algorithm and the use of no cut strengthening.\n\n## Master Problem Strengthening\n\nValid inequalities and enhanced Benders cuts are applied to strengthen the linear programming relaxation of the master problem. Additionally, researchers have investigated using Constraint Programming (CP) to solve the master problem in Logic-based Benders Decomposition, exploiting variable assignment bounds, variable assignment counting, and global constraints to construct combinatorial cut encodings.\n\nThe search results focus heavily on LBBD and combinatorial Benders cuts but do not specifically address RLT (Reformulation-Linearization Technique) cuts in the context you queried.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8b3099e2-4468-4b55-bf74-1a00fe88f754","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:48.174Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61e2ab50-8314-4d4a-beb1-ee1b68d69f08","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8b3099e2-4468-4b55-bf74-1a00fe88f754","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6c24b41b58cd6945","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016ebUhdzjvXEJkJ3FwKs5c8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me now produce the report.\n\n---\n\n# RLT 与 Lift-and-Project 在 2D Placement / 二次约束问题上的调研\n\n## 1. RLT 基础 + Sherali-Adams 层级\n\nRLT（Reformulation-Linearization Technique）由 Sherali 和 Adams 提出，是把 0-1 混合整数 / 多项式规划线性化到更紧 LP 松弛的统一框架。两阶段流程：\n- **Reformulation 阶段**：把原约束乘上由 0-1 变量 x_i 和 (1−x_i) 组成的\"乘子积\"，生成隐含的多项式约束\n- **Linearization 阶段**：把每个不同的乘积项 x_i·x_j（甚至 x_i·x_j·x_k）替换成新变量 w_ij，得到线性 LP\n\n层级 d=1, 2, …, n 给出从连续松弛一路到凸包的渐进相对偏序。**层级越高越紧，但变量数指数爆炸**：n 个 0-1 变量在层级 d 下需要 O(n^d) 新变量。\n对 0-1 二次问题（QAP/QAP-like），第 1 层 RLT (RLT1) 已经显著优于标准 LP 松弛；第 2 层 (RLT2) 进一步收紧，但内存爆炸（QAP-3 报告 700GB 级）。和 Lift-and-Project (Balas–Ceria–Cornuejols) 的关系：**RLT 支配 L&P 的单变量分裂**，因为 RLT 乘子是变量本身而非一般析取，能识别冗余和利用结构。\n\n## 2. 实用 RLT 工具\n\n- **RLT-POS**（Dalkiran & Sherali 2016, Math Programming Computation）：开源 Python+Fortran 库，专门解多项式规划。带 constraint filtering、reduced RLT、半正定切、bound-grid-factor。基准对比 BARON / COUENNE / SparsePOP，对中等规模 QAP/PolyOpt 表现稳定。\n- **Pyomo 生态**：**没有原生 RLT 扩展**。Pyomo.GDP 提供 Big-M / Hull / hybrid (Trespalacios-Grossmann) reformulation；McCormick 双线性松弛由 mc++ 或 OptimalRML 等第三方提供。如果要在 Pyomo 上做 RLT，得手工生成乘积约束。\n- **PySAT**：纯 SAT 工具栈，**不适用** RLT（RLT 是 LP/MIP 范畴）。问题里写的\"PySAT\"应是误记，正确应该是 RLT-POS 或 Gurobi/CPLEX 的非线性预处理。\n- **商业求解器**：Gurobi 11+ 和 CPLEX 在 NLP 预处理里隐式使用 RLT 风格的乘积线性化，但不暴露层级控制接口。\n\n## 3. CP-SAT add_rlt_cuts 参数\n\n`sat_parameters.proto` 里有：\n```\noptional bool add_rlt_cuts = 277 [default = true];\n```\nLaurent Perron 注释为\"experimental, helps on binary problems with a lot of clauses of size 3\"。**默认开启**，针对 SAT 层面的 3-clause 多项式结构生成 RLT 形式切。这是 SAT-LP hybrid 的轻量版 RLT，**不是完整 Sherali-Adams 层级**——只在 binary 子结构上动手。我们的项目已经隐式享受这个好处，无需额外配置。\n\n## 4. 对 Placement / Packing 的应用\n\n- **QAP（与 facility layout / placement 同族）**：RLT1 给出当前最强的 LP-based 下界之一。研究显示利用对称性（symmetry-exploiting RLT）可以把 RLT2 的内存压下去。\n- **Rectangle packing / 2D placement**：直接 RLT 应用很少。原因是布局问题的核心二次性是\"如果 i,j 都放置且重叠则…\"，这种 disjunctive 结构更适合用 no-overlap 约束（CP-SAT 原生）或 Big-M 析取，而不是显式乘积。RLT 在 placement 上的实用案例集中在：\n  - QAP 形式（位置-设施分配，流量×距离目标二次）\n  - 双线性容量约束（端口 i 接到位置 j，开关变量 × 流量）\n\n## 5. 与 Combinatorial Benders 的关系\n\nLBBD（logic-based Benders, 我们用的）和 RLT 是**正交但可组合**的两件事：\n- LBBD 的 master 弱在 LP 松弛粗糙，subproblem infeasibility 通过 no-good cut 反馈\n- RLT 切可以加进 master 的 LP 松弛，**收紧 master root LP bound**，从而减少需要枚举的整数节点\n- 文献（Operations Research Forum 2023 综述）指出 cut-strengthening 对 LBBD 收敛速度影响显著，irreducible cuts > greedy > none\n- 实际工程做法：在 master 加 RLT1 形式的乘积线性化（端口配对 × 设施开关），但要谨慎——RLT 切数量 O(n²) 可能拖慢每节点 LP\n\n---\n\n## 对我们项目可行性\n\n**不建议把完整 Sherali-Adams 层级搬进来**，理由如下：\n\n1. **CP-SAT 已经在用 RLT 风格切**（add_rlt_cuts 默认开启），我们已享其惠。\n2. **我们的二次性主要在 binding subproblem**（端口连接 × 设施位置），不在 master。Master 已是纯 0-1 placement，没有显式双线性。\n3. **手工注入 RLT1 切到 master**：理论上可做（端口配对乘积 → 新变量 w_ij），但工程代价高——266 mandatory × 70×70 = 1.3M 候选位置，RLT1 新变量量级会到 10^11，不现实。\n4. **可探索的窄路径**：在 binding subproblem 的 LP relax 上加 RLT1（端口数 ~ 几百，规模可控），或许能给 master 反馈更紧的可行性证书，缩短 Benders 迭代。属于 **Phase 3B Lane B 加速类微优化**，预期收益 5-15%，不是数量级提升。\n5. **RLT-POS 工具不适配**：它是面向 polynomial programming 的独立 solver，无法插入我们 CP-SAT + custom Benders 的架构。\n\n**结论：低优先级。**当前 S-stage 列表里没有 RLT 任务是正确的。如果未来 Phase 3C 要对 LP root bound 做收紧，再考虑在 binding subproblem 局部应用 RLT1，且必须遵守 AI 安全契约（hints-only，不当作证明源）。建议优先消化 Lane B/C 已有任务，RLT 留作长期 backlog。\n\nSources:\n- [RLT for MIPs (Sherali, Wiley)](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/9780470400531.eorms0712)\n- [Cutting planes for RLT relaxations of mixed 0-1 polynomial programs (Math Prog)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10107-015-0863-8)\n- [RLT insights into lift-and-project closures (Optimization Letters)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11590-014-0763-5)\n- [RLT-POS software (Dalkiran & Sherali, MPC 2016)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-016-0099-5)\n- [Symmetry in RLT-type relaxations for QAP (EJOR 2014)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221713008308)\n- [Strong RLT1 bounds from decomposable Lagrangean relaxation (Annals of OR)](https://ideas.repec.org/a/spr/annopr/v286y2020i1d10.1007_s10479-018-3092-8.html)\n- [or-tools sat_parameters.proto (add_rlt_cuts)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [CP-SAT Primer - Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [Computational Evaluation of Cut-Strengthening in LBBD (OR Forum 2023)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43069-023-00242-3)\n- [Combinatorial Benders' Cuts (Codato & Fischetti)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-25960-2_14)\n- [Pyomo.GDP ecosystem (Optimization and Engineering)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11081-021-09601-7)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5759,"cache_read_input_tokens":25599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5759,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyA2yHRemX1Rh31WV3t","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f69e0e0e-b1ff-42b5-af28-d155181c4858","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:46.668Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
